  "notes": "\"**The baile-funk grammar is the entry**\" — the research says so, and describes it: \"a syncopated tamborzão-derived kick-and-snare pattern (a repeating 3+3+2-adjacent figure rather than a 2&4 backbeat), dense layered hand percussion, and a metallic snare/rim as the accent voice\". So the kick carries a high `tresilloBias` on a straight 95–135 grid, the snare is pulled off the square backbeat with `offSnare`, the rim is a real lane and the perc block is dense. His stated influence from Kaytranada is \"bouncy… **hollow 808 drum/bass lines**\", and the entry turns that into the low-end parameter: \"a hollow, short, bouncy 808 with a fast decay that functions rhythmically rather than as a drone — the opposite of the lane's sustained-808 default, and the reason his placements sound distinct on a trap-soul album. Slides are short and used as accents.\" That is `sustain` `staccato`, a short `portamentoMs` and a moderate `slideProb` — the sharpest 808 contrast in this section against the drone models. \"His father witnessed house music's birth in Chicago, and a four-on-the-floor variant is in the vocabulary\" is `fourOnFloorInChorus`. Harmony is \"sample-inherited m9/maj9 fragments over 2-bar loops, harmonically incomplete and unresolved\". ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum number and the 808 figures; the entry marks specific tempo/drum values as idiom inference. ⚠ `confidence` is medium, mirroring the entry. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
